1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,200
What if everything you think you know
about Africa is wrong?

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,880
Africa is not one country.

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:11,520
It's not just desert and lions.

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:21,040
It is 54 countries, 2,000 languages, and
some of the most jaw-dropping facts on the
entire planet.

5
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:26,880
Stay with me because by the end of this
video you will never see Africa the same
way

6
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:30,000
again. Fact number one.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,560
Africa is massive.

8
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:40,160
Most people look at a world map and think
Africa looks average, medium-sized.

9
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:42,920
But that map is lying to you.

10
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,720
You could fit the United States inside
Africa.

11
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,480
Then add China.

12
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:50,440
Then add India.

13
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:56,120
Then add most of Europe, and Africa would
still have room left over.

14
00:00:56,120 --> 00:01:03,480
The continent covers over 30 million
square kilometers. It is the second
largest landmass on Earth,

15
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:08,440
and almost nobody realizes it. Fact number
two.

16
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:11,840
You think Egypt has the most pyramids in
the world.

17
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,920
Everyone does.

18
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:16,040
You are wrong.

19
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:22,920
Sudan has 223 pyramids. That is twice as
many as Egypt.

20
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:28,560
These are the Meroe pyramids built by the
ancient Nubian kingdom of Kush.

21
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:33,920
They are older, steeper, and more
mysterious than the ones in Giza.

22
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:39,360
And almost nobody in the Western world has
ever heard of them.

23
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:41,880
Fact number three.

24
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:45,600
Penguins live in Africa.

25
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:47,760
Not in a zoo.

26
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:54,920
In the wild. On the rocky coastline of
South Africa, there is a thriving colony
of African

27
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:58,960
penguins. And here is the best part.

28
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:05,040
They make a sound exactly like a donkey.

29
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:09,800
That is why locals call them jackass
penguins.

30
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:17,920
Seriously. Unfortunately, they are
endangered with fewer than 50,000 left in
the world.

31
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,480
Africa never stops surprising you.

32
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:23,480
Fact number four.

33
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:27,920
Africa is home to over 2,000 languages.

34
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:33,959
That is more than 25% of every language
spoken on Earth.

35
00:02:33,959 --> 00:02:41,880
Nigeria alone, one single country, has
over 500 living languages.

36
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:48,440
For comparison, the entire continent of
Europe has around 300.

37
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:51,880
Africa is not just geographically diverse.

38
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:57,720
It is the most linguistically rich place
in all of human history.

39
00:02:57,720 --> 00:03:00,880
Fact number five.

40
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:05,120
Elephants are the engineers of the African
savanna.

41
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:12,600
During drought, when rivers dry up and the
land turns to dust, elephants use their
tusks and trunks to

42
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:15,840
dig deep into dry riverbeds.

43
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:18,160
They create wells.

44
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:21,840
They can smell water from 12 miles away.

45
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:26,640
And when they find it, they dig until it
reaches the surface.

46
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:28,640
Then zebras drink.

47
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,519
Then antelope.

48
00:03:30,519 --> 00:03:40,040
Then birds. One elephant saves an entire
ecosystem every single drought season.

49
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:42,720
Fact number six.

50
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:46,680
Giraffes sleep for just 30 minutes a day.

51
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:54,640
30 minutes. They are the tallest animals
on Earth, up to 19 ft tall.

52
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:58,960
And yet they survive on less sleep than
almost any other mammal.

53
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:02,440
Lying down makes them an easy target for
lions.

54
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:08,920
So they rest standing up in short bursts,
always watching.

55
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:14,800
Imagine living your entire life on 30
minutes of sleep.

56
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:20,560
Giraffes do it every single day. Fact
number seven.

57
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:27,680
Every single human being on this planet
traces their DNA back to Africa.

58
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,520
Every person.

59
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:31,480
Every culture.

60
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:34,320
Every civilization.

61
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:41,160
The human lineage first appeared here over
4 million years ago.

62
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:44,760
Africa is not a distant foreign land.

63
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:47,600
It is not somewhere else.

64
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:52,520
It is home. It is where all of us began.

65
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:55,640
Scientists call it the motherland.

66
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:57,120
And they are right.

67
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:59,760
Fact number eight.

68
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:03,760
Africa is the wealthiest continent on
Earth.

69
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:08,760
Not in dollars, in what the Earth actually
holds.

70
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:18,280
Africa contains 90% of the world's
platinum reserves, 40% of its gold, and
60% of its cobalt,

71
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:25,400
the mineral that powers every smartphone
and every electric car battery on the
planet.

72
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:29,640
The world runs on Africa's resources.

73
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,440
It always has.

74
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:33,760
Fact number nine.

75
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:42,400
Every single year, 1 and 1/2 million
wildebeest begin the longest and most
dangerous journey on Earth.

76
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:53,560
500 miles across Tanzania and Kenya
through rivers filled with crocodiles,
past lions, cheetahs, and hyenas.

77
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,360
They follow the rain.

78
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:57,720
They follow the grass.

79
00:05:57,720 --> 00:06:00,440
Thousands die along the way.

80
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:03,920
And yet, they keep moving.

81
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:08,600
It is the greatest wildlife spectacle on
the face of the earth.

82
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:12,080
And it happens every single year.

83
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:16,680
Africa is not what the world has told you
it is.

84
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:19,240
It is ancient.

85
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:24,400
It is rich. It is diverse.

86
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:31,640
And it is the foundation of everything we
call human civilization.

87
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:37,560
If this video changed how you see Africa,
subscribe.

88
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:41,360
Because we are just getting started.

89
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:47,040
And drop a comment below, which fact
shocked you the most?

90
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:50,960
I read every single one.
